Make pillow's setup.py build against the cross target instead of the build
host. This is the older of the recipe's two patches: meta.yaml selects it for
anything below pillow 12, while setup-12.x.patch covers 12.x and later and is
what current builds use.

In practice the file matches pillow 10.x alone; all three hunks fail against
11.x, whose `initialize_options` grew a return annotation and whose
`get_macos_sdk_path` already passes `--sdk macosx` to xcrun. The 11.x-shaped
variant of this patch is what became setup-12.x.patch at the 12 bump, so
recover it from git history if an 11.x build is ever needed.

pillow does not ask the compiler what it can reach. Its `pil_build_ext`
collects candidate include and library directories itself, probes them for
zlib.h, libjpeg, libfreetype and the rest, and compiles in whatever it
believes it found, every probe running on the build machine.

  1. `disable_platform_guessing` is forced True instead of being read from
     setup.cfg. It is the master switch for the "add platform directories"
     chain and the "standard locations" block after it (/usr/local, /usr,
     /lib and the per-platform additions), and with it on nothing pillow
     stumbles over on the runner can switch itself on. The context here still
     carries `self.add_imaging_libs = ""`, the line 12.x removed and the
     whole reason the recipe keeps two patch files.

  2. `get_macos_sdk_path` becomes `get_apple_sdk_path` and works out which
     SDK to ask xcrun for from `sys.platform` together with the simulator
     suffix on `sys.implementation._multiarch`: iphoneos or iphonesimulator,
     appletvos or appletvsimulator, watchos or watchsimulator, and no
     argument at all for macOS. Unpatched, the method runs `xcrun
     --show-sdk-path` bare, which answers with the host macOS SDK whatever
     the target is.

  3. The darwin branch is routed through the renamed method, and a new
     `elif sys.platform in {"ios", "tvos", "watchos"}` branch contributes
     that SDK's usr/lib and usr/include.

     Both of those live in the elif chain headed by
     `if self.disable_platform_guessing: pass`, so point 1 makes them
     unreachable. It was not always so: the SDK work predates the forced
     flag, which arrived with Android cross-compiling and replaced an earlier
     revision's per-platform exclusion of the standard locations. Read points
     2 and 3 as the record of how an Apple SDK has to be selected, not as
     something this build executes.

Reviving this line for real use would mean porting back the two hunks the
file never grew: gating upstream's unconditional `sys.prefix/{lib,include}`
additions on platform guessing, and filtering host paths out of
`self.compiler.{include,library}_dirs` before feature probing. Both are in
setup-12.x.patch, explained there.

